# The published site, committed on purpose.
#
# Cloudflare Pages deploys straight from this repository, and the mirror cannot be
# built there: its inputs are the 1.9 GB unpacked backup in work/ and the 396 MB
# archive in 24.4.22-tftstar/, neither of which can live in a repository. So the build
# output is the artifact this repo carries, Pages is told to run no build command, and
# the deploy step is "rebuild locally, commit dist, push".
#
# dist/ is therefore generated content under version control. Never hand-edit it: the
# next run of node tools/mirror.mjs overwrites whatever is there.

# Scratch derived from the WordPress backup: the unpacked 1 GB docroot, the
# decompressed SQL dump, and a wp-config.php holding local database credentials.
# None of it belongs in a repository, and none of it is needed to build the site.
work/

# The backup itself, supplied as an input to the ingest rather than stored here.
24.4.22-tftstar/

# Owner-authored new-release material (573 MB of photos / videos / spec PDFs).
# Same shape as the backup: an input the build reads once and turns into
# data/new-products.json + dist/, neither of which needs the raw folder to stay
# on disk after that. The scanner errors out clearly if this folder is missing.
#
# Anchored to the repository root on purpose. Unanchored, a gitignore pattern
# matches at every depth, and the generated category pages are named after this
# very folder - `dist/product-category/新品发布/index.html` and its `/en/` twin
# were therefore ignored, never committed, and 404 in production while the disk
# and every local gate said they existed (2026-11-11). A source folder that
# shares its name with a page slug is not optional commentary: the pattern has
# to say where it applies.
/新品发布/

# The Friway design reference. It informed an earlier, abandoned build and is not part
# of this mirror, so shipping it would put someone else's template in the repo.
Template/

# dependencies
node_modules/

# logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# local env overrides
.env
.env.local

# editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
